{"id":"19B","title":"Judgment Guidelines","part":{"n":19,"title":"Judgment & execution of law"},"url":"/law/19-judgment-execution-of-law/19b","entries":[{"id":"19B.1","text":"The aim of judgments in civil disputes should be to justify the righteous and condemn the wicked.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":25,"verses":"1"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":6,"verses":"22-23"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":17,"verses":"15"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":18,"verses":"5"}],"citation":"Deut. 25:1; 2 Chron. 6:22-23; Prov. 17:15; Prov. 18:5."},{"id":"19B.2","text":"Judgments are to adhere to a just and standard system of weights, measurements, and balances.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":19,"verses":"35-36"}],"citation":"Lev. 19:35-36."},{"id":"19B.3","text":"Execute true judgment between man and man.","refs":[{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":18,"verses":"8"},{"book":"Zechariah","chapter":7,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Ezek. 18:8; Zech. 7:9."},{"id":"19B.4","text":"The man who will act presumptuously and will not listen to the proper authorities or the judges, should be put to death.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":17,"verses":"12-13"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":15,"verses":"30-31"}],"citation":"Deut. 17:12-13; Num. 15:30-31."},{"id":"19B.5","text":"Controversies are to be judged according to God's judgments.","refs":[{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":44,"verses":"24"}],"citation":"Ezek. 44:24."},{"id":"19B.6","text":"Judge not according to the outward appearance of things.","refs":[{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":16,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":23,"verses":"27-28"},{"book":"John","chapter":7,"verses":"24"},{"book":"2 Corinthians","chapter":10,"verses":"7"}],"citation":"1 Sam. 16:7; Matt. 23:27-28; John 7:24; 2 Cor. 10:7."},{"id":"19B.7","text":"Ignorance of a crime (or breaking a law unintentionally) does not excuse the crime or eliminate punishment.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":4,"verses":"27-28"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":5,"verses":"15-19"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":15,"verses":"27-28"}],"citation":"Lev. 4:27-28; Lev. 5:15-19; Num. 15:27-28."},{"id":"19B.8","text":"One who does anything unintentionally or out of ignorance is to be given a lighter sentence than a person who does anything defiantly or with outright contempt of the law.","refs":[{"book":"Numbers","chapter":15,"verses":"29-31"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":12,"verses":"47-48"}],"citation":"Num. 15:29-31; Luke 12:47-48."},{"id":"19B.9","text":"Fathers shall not be put to death for the crimes of their children, neither shall the children be put to death for the crimes of their father.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":24,"verses":"16"},{"book":"2 Kings","chapter":14,"verses":"6"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":25,"verses":"4"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":31,"verses":"29-30"},{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":18,"verses":"20"}],"citation":"Deut. 24:16; 2 Kings 14:6; 2 Chron. 25:4; Jer. 31:29-30; Ezek. 18:20."},{"id":"19B.10","text":"You shall not be afraid in any man's presence, for the judgment is God's.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":1,"verses":"17"}],"citation":"Deut. 1: 17."},{"id":"19B.11","text":"Do not show partiality in judgment.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":23,"verses":"3"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":19,"verses":"15"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":16,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":24,"verses":"23"}],"citation":"Exod. 23:3; Lev. 19:15; Deut 16:19; Prov. 24:23."}]}